[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong and what I changed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C code uses preprocessor macros [38;5;10mOP[0m and [38;5;10mREPEAT[0m that are set at compile time via [38;5;10m-DOP=mul -DREPEAT=4[0m (derived from the variant name [38;5;10mmacrodepth_mul_4[0m). The CMakeLists.txt has defaults of [38;5;10madd[0m/[38;5;10m5[0m, but the actual test configuration uses [38;5;10mmul[0m/[38;5;10m4[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The LLM that produced the Rust translation used the wrong macro values — it hardcoded everything for [38;5;10mOP=add[0m with [38;5;10mREPEAT=5[0m instead of [38;5;10mOP=mul[0m with [38;5;10mREPEAT=4[0m. This caused three categories of errors:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1mWrong operation[22m: All calls used [38;5;10mop_add[0m (a+b) instead of [38;5;10mop_mul[0m (a*b)[0m[0m
2. [1mWrong accumulator initial value[22m: [38;5;10mINIT_add = 0[0m was used instead of [38;5;10mINIT_mul = 1[0m[0m[0m
3. [1mWrong step logic[22m: [38;5;10mSTEP_add(acc, i)[0m does [38;5;10macc += i[0m, while [38;5;10mSTEP_mul(acc, i)[0m does [38;5;10macc *= (i + 1)[0m — completely different semantics[0m[0m
4. [1mWrong REPEAT count[22m: [38;5;10mrun_loop[0m unrolled 5 iterations (indices 0–4) instead of 4 (indices 0–3), and [38;5;10muse_generated[0m was called with [38;5;10m5[0m instead of [38;5;10m4[0m[0m[0m
5. [1mWrong op name in output[22m: Printed [38;5;10m"add"[0m instead of [38;5;10m"mul"[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The fix changed every occurrence to use [38;5;10mmul[0m semantics: multiplication operation, initial accumulator of [38;5;10m1[0m, step logic [38;5;10macc *= (i + 1)[0m, 4 unrolled iterations, and the correct op name string.[0m[0m
